# Local chat model for the Edu Platform (tutor answers, flashcard/question/roadmap JSON).
# Build:  npm run llm:setup   (or: ollama create edu-chat -f ollama/edu-chat.Modelfile)
#
# qwen3:4b-instruct (Q4_K_M, 2.5 GB) answers directly, without hidden "thinking" tokens, and
# fits in RAM on a CPU-only laptop. Measured on an i7-13620H: prompt reading ~85 tokens/s,
# writing ~12-14 tokens/s, so a tutor answer takes ~20 s and a flashcard call ~40 s.
#
# Why a custom model instead of plain qwen3:4b-instruct: Ollama's OpenAI-compatible /v1 endpoint
# cannot set the context window per request, and its 4096-token default is too small for a
# 3-chunk generation prompt plus its JSON answer. Sampling (temperature) stays per request.
FROM qwen3:4b-instruct
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER num_predict 2048
